{		[VMSLIB] on the VAX/VMS masterpack on STAR::.
{
{		Old audit trail follows......
{
{		========================================================
{
{     X-3,4,5   MAS		Mary A. Sullivan	13-Feb-1992
{	        Merge in changes from variant stream in VMSLIB facility.
{	        reset the ident now that we're in STARLET.
{
{		========================================================
{
{     X-6X3     WDA             W.D. Arbo               18-Dec-1991
{               Delete the E(S)GPS$V_PAG bit, moving the E(S)GPS$V_COMM
{               and E(S)GPS$V_NOMOD bits so that they are in the same
{               relative positions on VAX and Alpha.
{
{               Remove VECTOR_TYPE_INCREMENT and MASK_TYPE_INCREMENT
{               from $EGSDEF.
{
{     X-6X2     WDA             W.D. Arbo               06-Dec-1991
{               Fix comments for STC_LP_PSB.
{
{
{     X-6X1     WDA             W.D. Arbo               02-Nov-1991
{               Add new store-conditional ETIR commands, expand the
{               ESDF records to include the CODE_ADDRESS and CA_PSINDX
{               fields.  Create a new EGSD record EGST for use in
{               global symbol tables.  The EGST has fields which allow
{               the contents of the symbol vector to be redulplicated.
{ 
{               ESDF$L_CODE_ADDRESS and ESDF$L_CA_PSINDX fields will 
{               only be valid when the EGSY$V_NORM bit is set.  Otherwise 
{               they must be zero.  The ESDF$L_CODE_ADDRESS contains the 
{               offset into the psect indicated by ESDF$L_CA_PSINDX of the entry 
{               for the procedure signified by the name string.
{
{               The EGST$ record, which the linker will use for universal symbol
{               definitions in global symbol tables of shareable images, has the
{               linkage pair fields, but generically labeled LP_1 and LP_2, since
{               their contents are different depending on whether the symbol
{               is a procedure (LP_1=code address, LP_2=procedure descriptor address),
{               a data cell (LP_1=0, LP_2=data cell address) or a constant (LP_1 = 0,
{               LP_2 = constant value).  The LP_1 and LP_2 fields in the EGST 
{               reduplicate the contents of the symbol vector. {
{
{               Add EEOM$L_TOTAL_LPS field to the end-of-module record.
{               This lists the total number of linkage pairs in the image.
{               Since each linkage pair has two indices, one pointing to the
{               first quadword and another to the second, this number should
{               equal the second index of the highest linkage pair divided by 2.
{
{               Bump the structure level for Alpha to 2.
{
{     X-6       WDA             W.D. Arbo               02-Nov-1991
{               Back out EGSY$V_SYMVECT pending decision on whether
{               to implement link-time constants.
{
{     X-5       WDA             W.D. Arbo               31-Oct-1991
{               Add EGSY$V_SYMVECT.  This flag indicates whether 
{               an EGSD record in an Alpha shareable image's GST has a 
{               corresponding entry in the symbol vector.  This 
{               flag is being used to implement link-time constants
{               on Alpha.
{
{               TS              Todd Schoeller          30-Oct-1991
{               Propogate the NOMOD and COM psect flags to Alpha structures.
{               These were merged into the VAX structures in X-10K3, but they 
{               were not added to the Alpha structures.
{
{     X-4       WDA0194         W.D. Arbo               25-Jun-1991
{               Add new store command for linkage pairs with 
{               a procedure signature block (ETIR$C_STO_LP_PSB)
{
{     X-3       WDA0171         W.D. Arbo               23-Apr-1991
{               Add EOBJ$C_EDBG and EOBJ$C_ETBT - do not increment
{               structure level.
{
{     X-10K6    WDA0160         W.D. Arbo               22-Jan-1991
{               Rename STO_IMM as STO_IMMR.  Add new STO_IMM and
{               STO_GBL_LW.  Bump the STRLVL.
{
{     X-10K5    DLM             Dan Murphy              26-Sep-1990
{               Fix long comments lines which were crashing SDL.
{
{     X-10K4	LWW		Larry Woodman		24-Aug-1990
{		Fix ALPHA symm and symv
{
{     X-10K3    WDA0112         W.D. Arbo                20-Aug-1990
{               Fold in changes from VMS generation 11:
{
{	        X-11	        PSW001 Paul S. Winalski  17-Jul-1990
{		Add GPS$V_COM to support COMM symbols and GPS$V_NOMOD for
{		possible future use.
{
{               Fix documentation of STO_OFF, and correct version history
{               (X-12 changed to X-10K2)
{
{     X-10K2    LWW0000          Larry Woodman           30-JUL-1990
{                               (Dan Murphy
{                                W.D. Arbo)
{
{               Add new modules to define object file format for ALPHA/EVMS.
{               These new modules have names with an E appended (e.g. 
{               $EOBJRECDEF).
{
{
{	X-10	ROW0625		Ralph O. Weber		10-MAR-1988 17:24
{		Eliminate usage of GLOBAL_ENTRY_POINT_RECORD name on two
{		structure statements so that BASIC can use the SDL output
{		without getting multiply defined symbols of the form
{		OBJ$R_GLOBAL_ENTRY_POINT_RECORD.
{
{	X-9	DLM004		Dan Murphy		16-Apr-1987
{		Add GSY$V_COMM for possible future use.
{
{	X-8	DLM001		Dan Murphy		09-Jan-1987
{		Correct comments for vectored symbol and mask symbol
{		records.
{
{	X-7	SF04001		Stephen Fiorelli	08-Dec-1986
{		Add some more definitions for new address/mask
{		double valued symbols to $OBJRECDEF.
{
{	X-6	MJW0073		Michael J. Worcester	05-Dec-1986
{		Add symbols to $OBJRECDEF as follows:
{
{			1. PSECT_RECORD symbols
{			2. GLOBAL_SYM_RECORD symbols
{			3. ENTRY_POINT_RECORD symbols
{			4. GLOBAL_SYMV_RECORD symbols
{			5. GLOBAL_ENTRY_POINT_RECORD symbols
{			6. EOM_RECORD symbols
{
{		These symbols were moved from $OBJDEF in SDADEF.SDL
{		in facility SDA.  $OBJDEF symbols in SDA have been
{		removed from SDADEF.SDL .  Also added TYPE_OVERLAY
{		symbols OBJ$B_TYPE and OBJ$B_GSD_TYPE.
{
{	X-5	MJW0068		Michael J. Worcester	20-Nov-1986
{		Add symbols OBJ$C_GSD_SYMV, OBJ$C_GSD_EPMV,
{		OBJ$C_GSD_PROV to maintain consistency with $GSDEF
{		symbols for SDA's benefit.
{
{	X-4	JWT0263		Jim Teague		11-Nov-1986
{		Add constant for changing GSD type from regular type
{		to VECTOR or MASK type.  For example:
{
{		GSD$C_SYMM = GSD$V_SYM + GSD$C_MASK_TYPE_INCREMENT
{
{	X-3	JWT0257		Jim Teague		21-Oct-1986
{		Add $SDFMDEF, $EPMMDEF, and $PROMDEF.  These defn's
{		are similar to the vectored ones below, but the
{		"second" value of the symbol is a mask, rather than
{		an offset in a transfer array.
{
{	X-2	JWT0207		Jim Teague		10-Jul-1985
{		Add $SDFVDEF, $EPMVDEF, $PROVDEF structures.  
{		They are vectored-symbol equivalents 
{		to the similarly-named structures without
{		the "V" before the "DEF".  These structures allow a
{		second value (the "vectored" value) for symbol 
{		entries in a "vectored" image.
{
{	V03-005	JWT0113		Jim Teague		27-Apr-1983
{		Another new type for the Linker Options Record,
{		LNK$C_SHA, for individually specified shr imgs.
{
{	V03-004	JWT0102		Jim Teague		16-Mar-1983
{		Add a new type to the Linker Options Record, LNK$C_OBJ.
{
{	V03-003	JWT0082		Jim Teague		20-Dec-1982
{		Add V_NESTED to environment flags to clear up the
{		ambiguity of parent environment zero.
{
{	V03-002	ACG0303		Andrew C. Goldstein,	9-Dec-1982  16:02
{		Add FILL attribute to extraneous field names
{
{	V03-001		JWT0037		Jim Teague		18-Jun-1982
{		Add spec for linker options record (LNK)
{
{	V02-008		BLS0096		Benn Schreiber		31-Oct-1981
{		Add shareable image psect type SGPS
{
{	V02-007		BLS0094		Benn Schreiber		31-Oct-1981
{		Add STA_LEPM
{
{	V02-006		BLS0084		Benn Schreiber		21-Sep-1981
{		Make IDC IDMATCH 2 bits, add ERRSEV
{
{	V02-005		BLS0062		Benn Schreiber		28-Jul-1981
{		Correct local symbol definition
{
{	V02-004		BLS0045		Benn Schreiber		14-Mar-1981
{		Correct store repeated limit to be longword
{
{	V02-003		BLS0037		Benn Schreiber		29-Jan-1981
{		Add rest of new object language commands: local symbols,
{		end of module word psect.
{
{	V02-002		BLS0033		Benn Schreiber		5-Jan-1981
{		Add new definitions for more psects, add literal operators,
{		and ident check.
{
{	V02-001		BLS0011		Benn Schreiber		1-Sep-1980
{		Implement TIR$C_CTL_STKDL to stack debug location.
